1
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,200
I'll look through
the window first.

2
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:19,833
And if the coast
is clear, I'll knock.

3
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:24,700
If it isn't, then I'll stop
being obsessed with him. Okay?

4
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:26,700
[WOMAN] I finished changing.

5
00:00:26,833 --> 00:00:28,767
[GASPS]

6
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,200
- What is it?
- Girl--

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,267
You shouldn't waste
your tears on that guy.

8
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:36,067
There's nothing
wrong with you.

9
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,100
They're in the wrong
for leaving you.

10
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:40,033
For abandoning you.

11
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:41,500
And I'm just like them.

12
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:44,033
I think Jaja was really hurt
by what that person did.

13
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:45,100
Of course, she was, man.

14
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:46,800
What if someone
left you hanging

15
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:47,933
and started dating
someone else?

16
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:49,333
Ouch!

17
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:51,167
All I'm saying is, man...

18
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,967
We should help her move on.

19
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,900
Wa-Wait, hold on!

20
00:00:56,033 --> 00:00:58,067
Wait, Emma, erase that!

21
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,033
- Why should I?
- What? Why?

22
00:01:00,167 --> 00:01:01,633
It doesn't look good.

23
00:01:01,767 --> 00:01:04,533
Seriously? You also
don't think I look good?

24
00:01:04,667 --> 00:01:07,133
Jaja, I didn't mean you.
It's your clothes.

25
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,567
Could you please not judge me?

26
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:12,133
I need this.

27
00:01:12,267 --> 00:01:14,633
My followers need
to see that I'm okay

28
00:01:14,767 --> 00:01:16,633
and I'm not depressed.

29
00:01:16,767 --> 00:01:18,233
Because right now?

30
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:21,500
I feel like
I'm such an ugly person.

31
00:01:21,633 --> 00:01:23,433
I just need some...

32
00:01:23,567 --> 00:01:27,367
just a bit of affirmation
that I'm still beautiful.

33
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,767
That I'm not
that easy to replace.

34
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:31,400
Jaja, you are irreplaceable.

35
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:35,667
If someone sees you as such,
then they're blind.

36
00:01:37,233 --> 00:01:39,533
Because they don't see
your true worth.

37
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:46,533
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:54,767
[ROMANTIC MUSIC FADES]

39
00:01:59,033 --> 00:02:03,833
Wilberto... Wilberto...

40
00:02:03,967 --> 00:02:05,767
Girl, his name is so common.

41
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:07,267
There are so many
search results!

42
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:12,767
- [TAPPING ON TABLET]
- Wilberto... De Guzman...

43
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:16,300
World War Two, Philippines.

44
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:22,133
Hmm... What if...

45
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:23,733
Why don't we
add Nadia's name

46
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:25,567
so we can narrow it down?

47
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:27,933
- Great idea.
- Alright.

48
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:31,500
- Nadia...
- ...Cruz.

49
00:02:33,767 --> 00:02:35,333
Hm...

50
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:37,933
Find anything?

51
00:02:38,067 --> 00:02:43,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,767
"Nadia Cruz won't talk about

53
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:49,733
her brother who abandoned her
during the war."

54
00:02:50,967 --> 00:02:52,433
Uh...

55
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:56,533
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

56
00:02:56,667 --> 00:02:59,600
"Her brother is the brave,
but forgotten hero

57
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:02,867
from Quezon Province,
Wilberto de Guzman.

58
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:08,800
Wilberto joined
the guerilla fighters

59
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:11,800
to fight off the invaders."

60
00:03:13,133 --> 00:03:15,300
[DEEP, NERVOUS BREATHS]

61
00:03:16,233 --> 00:03:19,600
[DEEP, NERVOUS BREATHS]

62
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:23,633
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:27,767
Son, never forget what you
promised your mother and I.

64
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:32,167
Never leave your sister
whatever happens.

65
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,800
Yes, Papa. I promise.

66
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,467
Hide yourselves.
Hide now!

67
00:03:42,167 --> 00:03:45,033
- [SCREAMING]
- [BLOW LANDS]

68
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:46,600
[SCREAMING]

69
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:49,333
[GUNSHOTS]

70
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:54,700
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [DISTANT SCREAMS]

71
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:57,367
[SNIFFLES]

72
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,800
- Nadia?
- [SNIFFLES]

73
00:03:59,933 --> 00:04:03,200
Don't cry, okay?
I will never leave you.

74
00:04:05,967 --> 00:04:07,600
I promise you that, okay?

75
00:04:09,467 --> 00:04:10,333
[JAJA] "But to Nadia,

76
00:04:10,467 --> 00:04:12,700
that old wound is still fresh.

77
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:15,300
"A true hero would
have never left behind

78
00:04:15,433 --> 00:04:17,200
the last of his family,

79
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:20,867
especially in the midst
of tragedy," Nadia added.

80
00:04:22,267 --> 00:04:24,333
- [GUNSHOT]
- [DISTANT SCREAM]

81
00:04:28,567 --> 00:04:34,133
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:04:34,267 --> 00:04:35,967
The two of us
were the last ones, man.

83
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,800
I tried to protect her.

84
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,800
As much as I could.

85
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:48,300
I even joined
the guerrilla fighters

86
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,800
to help drive away
the invaders

87
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:53,467
and end the war.

88
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:57,267
That way, I could
give her a decent life.

89
00:05:01,967 --> 00:05:03,000
But while that happened,

90
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,567
I became very strict with her.

91
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,600
That was probably why
she got so angry with me.

92
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:15,533
That was the last thing
we argued about.

93
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:19,900
After that...

94
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:23,167
I never got to return.

95
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:29,800
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:34,733
[JAJA] "Unfortunately, like our
other brave heroes...

97
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:39,500
It's as if Wilberto de Guzman
was erased from our history.

98
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:44,867
There barely exists any
records about his heroism,

99
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,867
about how he defended a small
town until his dying breath."

100
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,667
[SIGHS] Wow.

101
00:05:53,733 --> 00:05:56,033
Gosh, girl.

102
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:59,067
Turns out, Wilberto's a hero.

103
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,600
Awesome! At least we're
friends with a hero, right?

104
00:06:03,667 --> 00:06:05,633
Although, an obscure one
that no one knows about.

105
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:10,467
Maybe that's why his sister
is so angry with him.

106
00:06:10,633 --> 00:06:12,500
She probably thought
he abandoned her.

107
00:06:12,633 --> 00:06:14,833
But what if he really did?

108
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:18,467
I mean, we've had heroes
with cancel-worthy behaviors.

109
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:21,900
Like Jose Rizal,
who was a womanizer.

110
00:06:22,033 --> 00:06:24,000
Juan Luna was a wife killer.

111
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:27,700
So... Wilberto could really
have ghosted his sister.

112
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:32,633
You have a point, bestie.
But I don't think he did it.

113
00:06:33,933 --> 00:06:36,267
I still believe
he didn't mean to leave Nadia.

114
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:37,600
Because imagine...

115
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:39,933
Would he put in
this much effort,

116
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:42,633
talking to random strangers,

117
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,467
just to reach out to her
even after death?

118
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,600
[SMACKS LIPS]

119
00:06:46,733 --> 00:06:50,400
Well, there's only
one way to find out.

120
00:06:52,567 --> 00:06:54,533
I've wasted
so much time, girl.

121
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:59,400
My issue is nothing
compared to Wilberto's.

122
00:06:59,533 --> 00:07:00,967
Instead of helping
him out immediately,

123
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:03,600
I prioritized that damned
ex-boyfriend of mine.

124
00:07:03,733 --> 00:07:06,900
Oh, girl, don't invalidate
your feelings.

125
00:07:07,033 --> 00:07:09,933
That's a no-no for me, okay?
You know my feelings on that.

126
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:13,733
Anyway...

127
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,433
I need your help
with Grandma tomorrow.

128
00:07:15,567 --> 00:07:16,900
- Sure.
- That way...

129
00:07:17,033 --> 00:07:19,167
we could go search
for Nadia tomorrow.

130
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,833
Alright.

131
00:07:20,967 --> 00:07:22,267
I've got you.

132
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:29,433
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:07:57,733 --> 00:07:59,400
You sure you don't
need help with that?

134
00:07:59,533 --> 00:08:01,300
I can handle it.
Thanks for letting me stay.

135
00:08:01,433 --> 00:08:03,633
Wait, wait, wait.
Hold on. Hold your horses.

136
00:08:03,767 --> 00:08:06,767
I've changed my mind.
You're not going.

137
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:10,933
Grandma, that will make it
harder for us to leave.

138
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,333
That's why I'm doing it.

139
00:08:12,467 --> 00:08:14,400
Our bonding time is too short.

140
00:08:14,533 --> 00:08:15,633
It's still your
vacation, Janine.

141
00:08:15,767 --> 00:08:18,533
Why are you
in a rush to leave?

142
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,233
- [GIRLS STUTTER]
- [MALOU] Oh...

143
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:25,400
Don't tell me it's because
of your ex-boyfriend again.

144
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:27,400
Wha-- Grandma, no!

145
00:08:27,533 --> 00:08:29,400
- He's an ex. Red flag.
- He's my ex, Grandma.

146
00:08:29,533 --> 00:08:31,967
Um, there's-- There's
something we need to do.

147
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:33,633
- We have something to do.
- Yes, right.

148
00:08:33,767 --> 00:08:35,500
Also, Grandma,
don't you worry.

149
00:08:35,633 --> 00:08:37,567
If Jaja here does
something stupid,

150
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:38,833
I'll tell you immediately.

151
00:08:38,967 --> 00:08:40,800
- Hm... Really?
- Yes, of course.

152
00:08:40,933 --> 00:08:43,633
And, Grandma,
like I told you last night,

153
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:46,333
it will help me
move on faster if I leave.

154
00:08:46,467 --> 00:08:47,500
- [CHUCKLES]
- All right.

155
00:08:47,633 --> 00:08:49,133
Oh, be careful, you two, hm?

156
00:08:49,267 --> 00:08:51,400
- We will. Thank you.
- Yes.

157
00:08:51,533 --> 00:08:54,000
- I'll miss you two.
- Bye, Grandma.

158
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,500
Let's keep
in touch, Grandma.

159
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:58,200
- Huh?
- Of course.

160
00:08:58,333 --> 00:09:00,767
I have your number saved.

161
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,633
- Stay out of trouble, hm?
- I will.

162
00:09:02,767 --> 00:09:03,967
I'll take care of her.
Don't worry.

163
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,467
Tell me if
she gets into trouble.

164
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,300
- I'll text you immediately.
- Make sure you do.

165
00:09:07,433 --> 00:09:10,367
She knows he's a red flag now.

166
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,767
Could you introduce us
to your grandmother?

167
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,500
- Negative.
- What's negative?

168
00:09:14,633 --> 00:09:16,767
Ah! Right, yeah...

169
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:19,067
Grandma, it's uh...
Vhal's a negative topic to me.

170
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,833
- That's right, Grandma.
- He's a negative.

171
00:09:20,967 --> 00:09:22,400
Major negative vibes
from him.

172
00:09:22,533 --> 00:09:24,400
Hello, Grandma,
even if you can't see us.

173
00:09:24,533 --> 00:09:26,100
- Hmm...
- What-- What's that?

174
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,367
- Whoo!
- Oh, it's so hot!

175
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,733
Yes, girly pop! It's so hot!

176
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,867
- Come on. Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

177
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,800
Grandma, turn on the fan.
It's really hot, okay?

178
00:09:32,933 --> 00:09:35,500
- I will, I will.
- Okay, Grandma. Thanks again.

179
00:09:35,633 --> 00:09:37,000
- Hey, don't forget.
- Yes, I'll text you.

180
00:09:37,133 --> 00:09:38,600
It's usually respectful
to introduce

181
00:09:38,733 --> 00:09:40,067
your friends to your
parents or elders.

182
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:43,033
If I did that,
she wouldn't let me go at all.

183
00:09:43,167 --> 00:09:44,767
Even if she can't see us,

184
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,700
it's still not right for you
to not introduce us.

185
00:09:46,833 --> 00:09:48,867
That way, she wouldn't
worry as much, right?

186
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,033
She'll freak out that I'm
with a mumu (ghost).

187
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:54,767
What mumu ?
Who are you talking to?

188
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:57,533
- Ah! She's talking to me.
- I was talking to Emma.

189
00:09:57,667 --> 00:09:59,033
Girly pop-- I mean...

190
00:09:59,167 --> 00:10:01,133
- [BOTH] Mumu! (Ghostie!)
- We call each other that now.

191
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:02,433
- Ghostie...
- Ghostie?

192
00:10:02,567 --> 00:10:03,533
Bye, Grandma. Love you!

193
00:10:03,667 --> 00:10:05,900
- I think it's time to go...
- [BOTH] Ghostie!

194
00:10:06,033 --> 00:10:09,067
Let's go, girly pop--
I mean, ghostie! Ghostie.

195
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,833
- Yeah!
- They call themselves that?

196
00:10:11,967 --> 00:10:15,233
That's what we used to call
those long, flowy dresses.

197
00:10:19,733 --> 00:10:21,300
- Hi, ma'am! Back so soon?
- Hi, mister!

198
00:10:21,433 --> 00:10:24,033
We're back with a vengeance!

199
00:10:24,167 --> 00:10:25,133
Oh, how have you been?

200
00:10:25,267 --> 00:10:27,067
We're going to leave
our bags in our room, okay?

201
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,800
Then we'll go
to your sister's house.

202
00:10:28,933 --> 00:10:30,867
Come on, let's go
to the common area.

203
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,700
Ma'am, we aren't allowed
in the common area.

204
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:36,400
Ah! Yes, yes. Hello?
I'm on the phone with someone.

205
00:10:36,567 --> 00:10:37,933
Yeah, we're going up
to the common area.

206
00:10:38,067 --> 00:10:40,167
Okay. Bye-bye.
All right.

207
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:41,900
[EMMA] Ah.

208
00:10:43,567 --> 00:10:46,067
Psst! Hey! What are you--

209
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:49,600
Ah... [AWKWARD CHUCKLE]
Sorry, I didn't mean to...

210
00:10:49,733 --> 00:10:51,633
- You're so beautiful. Sexy.
- She's very pretty.

211
00:10:51,767 --> 00:10:54,100
- Ooh...
- Psst, come on.

212
00:10:54,233 --> 00:10:55,500
[SUITCASE THUDDING]

213
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:57,167
Why have you been
silent this whole time?

214
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,500
[SUITCASE THUDDING]

215
00:10:58,633 --> 00:11:00,067
We should--
We should introduce

216
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,967
ourselves properly
to my sister later.

217
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:03,167
[JAJA SNICKERS]

218
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:05,733
Like we should've done
at your grandmother's earlier.

219
00:11:05,867 --> 00:11:10,467
Oh, for the love of...
You're still stuck on that?

220
00:11:10,633 --> 00:11:11,867
She would've just freaked out.

221
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,267
She might think
I've gone cray-cray.

222
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,633
Oh, you don't know
what cray-cray means, huh?

223
00:11:17,767 --> 00:11:18,933
Cray-cray...
You don't get it?

224
00:11:19,067 --> 00:11:21,800
Like you, from head to toe.

225
00:11:21,933 --> 00:11:24,800
You know, you're lucky that
everyone's on vacation.

226
00:11:24,933 --> 00:11:28,933
Otherwise, people would think
that I'm talking to thin air.

227
00:11:29,067 --> 00:11:31,933
[DESCENDS INTO LAUGHTER,
LAUGHING SILENTLY]

228
00:11:32,067 --> 00:11:34,833
[INHALES LOUDLY]
Me, talking to thin air?

229
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:36,733
- [LAUGHING SILENTLY]
- [SLAPS SUITCASE HANDLE]

230
00:11:36,867 --> 00:11:39,533
[LAUGHING SILENTLY]

231
00:11:39,667 --> 00:11:42,233
I'm happy to see you smiling.

232
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,133
[SLOW GASP]

233
00:11:56,533 --> 00:12:02,933
["KINAKABAHAN" BY LILY
PLAYING]

234
00:12:03,067 --> 00:12:04,600
Thank you.

235
00:12:04,733 --> 00:12:07,733
And thanks
for the distraction.

236
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,867
[EMMA CLEARS HER THROAT]

237
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:16,600
Ma'am... Could I also
distract you for a bit?

238
00:12:16,767 --> 00:12:18,633
Bestie, I didn't
see you there!

239
00:12:18,767 --> 00:12:20,233
- Bestie!
- You didn't say anything!

240
00:12:20,367 --> 00:12:23,133
- I've been waiting for you!
- Oh, really now?

241
00:12:23,267 --> 00:12:25,700
- You forgot about me, hm?
- Uh, we'll go upstairs, okay?

242
00:12:25,833 --> 00:12:26,767
- You sure?
- Yeah.

243
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:29,133
Maybe you'd like
to stay longer?

244
00:12:29,267 --> 00:12:32,367
- You know, for...
- [TONY] Hey... Why?

245
00:12:33,567 --> 00:12:35,200
